text = "[color=#FFFFFF]
[font_size=28][color=#FF3B3B]Overview[/color][/font_size]
OutLIAR is a multiplayer social-deduction game aboard a deep-space vessel. Most of the players are Crew trying to keep the ship running. Hidden among them are [color=#FF3B3B]Imposters[/color] who lie, sabotage, and pick off the Crew one by one.

[font_size=28][color=#FF3B3B]Roles[/color][/font_size]
• [color=#9FB3C8]Crew[/color]: complete tasks around the ship and figure out who is lying.
• [color=#FF3B3B]Imposters[/color]: blend in with the Crew, fake tasks, and eliminate players without getting caught. The host chooses 1, 2, or 3 Imposters depending on lobby size.

[font_size=28][color=#FF3B3B]Objective[/color][/font_size]
• [color=#9FB3C8]Crew wins[/color] by eliminating every Imposter, or by surviving until the round timer runs out.
• [color=#FF3B3B]Imposters win[/color] by eliminating the Crew, or by sabotaging the ship until its integrity drops to zero.

[font_size=28][color=#FF3B3B]How a Round Works[/color][/font_size]
1. Players spawn on the ship and roles are dealt secretly.
2. Crew moves through the decks completing tasks and watching for suspicious behavior. Imposters fake tasks, trigger sabotages, and look for openings to strike.
3. If you find a body, you can report it. A report just alerts the rest of the ship that someone has died, there is no emergency meeting and no voting.
4. Crew tracks down Imposters and eliminates them, while Imposters pick off Crew and chip away at ship integrity.
5. The round ends the moment one side meets its win condition, or the timer expires in the Crew's favor.

[font_size=28][color=#FF3B3B]Controls[/color][/font_size]
• [color=#9FB3C8]W / A / S / D[/color]: move
• [color=#9FB3C8]Space[/color]: jump
• [color=#9FB3C8]E[/color]: interact (tasks, buttons, doors, pickups)
• [color=#9FB3C8]B[/color]: open the emote wheel, then press 1, 2, or 3 to play Flair, Breakdance, or Thriller
• [color=#9FB3C8]M[/color]: toggle your microphone on or off (a MIC MUTED indicator appears in the bottom-left when muted)
• [color=#9FB3C8]Mouse[/color]: look around

[font_size=28][color=#FF3B3B]Ship Systems[/color][/font_size]
• [color=#9FB3C8]Armory[/color]: the armory door is locked by default and holds the most powerful weapons on the ship, including the [color=#FF3B3B]taser[/color]. Opening it is a three-person job: two players have to stand at the left and right armory buttons and hold them down at the same time, while a third player runs inside to grab the gear. The door stays open only while both buttons are held, so coordinate before anyone steps in.
• [color=#9FB3C8]Elevator[/color]: each deck has a call button. Walk up and press E on it to call the elevator to your floor, then ride it between the upper and lower decks.
• [color=#9FB3C8]Security Cameras[/color]: certain stations let the Crew watch other parts of the ship. Use them to track movement and catch Imposters in the act.
• [color=#9FB3C8]Batons[/color]: scattered around the map. Walk up to one and press E to pick it up. Batons are the basic melee weapon, so even players who never make it into the armory have a way to fight back.
• [color=#9FB3C8]Health Packs[/color]: pick them up with E to restore health if you have been wounded.
• [color=#9FB3C8]Voice Chat[/color]: proximity voice is on while alive, so people near you can hear what you say. Dead players can still talk to other dead players in a separate channel. Press [color=#9FB3C8]M[/color] at any time to mute or unmute your microphone.

[font_size=28][color=#FF3B3B]Tips[/color][/font_size]
• Pay attention to where players come from. Alibis fall apart fast on a small ship.
• Watch task animations. A real task takes time, a fake one is instant.
• Use emotes (B) to celebrate, distract, or call out a play to your teammates.
• Buddy up around the armory. Imposters cannot open it alone, so getting weapons takes trust.
[/color]"

